public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.RelativeDegreeOne
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjPoint.AlgebraicSpace
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjRepresentsGenerated

/-!
# The functor `F₁` of triples on the constructed relative Proj of an algebraic space

In Situation 0849 let `P = Proj_X(𝒜)` be the relative homogeneous spectrum of Stacks 084A–084B,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.relativeProjFunctor`. Stacks 085D (1) says that
when `𝒜` is generated by `𝒜₁` over `𝒜₀`, `P` represents the functor `F₁` which sends `T` to the
isomorphism classes of triples `(f, ℒ, ψ)`: a morphism `f : T → X`, an invertible `𝒪_T`-module
`ℒ`, and a map of graded `𝒪_T`-algebras `ψ : f^*𝒜 → ⨁_{n ≥ 0} ℒ^{⊗ n}` surjective in degree one.

This file constructs `F₁` as a functor on the big fppf site and a natural morphism `F₁ ⟶ P`,
injective with no hypothesis on `𝒜`. That it is an isomorphism under the source's hypothesis is
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.RelativeProjF1Represents`.

* **The functor.** Its value at `T` is the set of pairs of a `T`-point `f` of `X` and a strict
  isomorphism class of pairs `(ℒ, ψ)` for the restriction `f^*𝒜`
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.F1`). Restriction along `τ : T' ⟶ T` pulls the
  triple back along `τ` and reads it over the restricted point through the identification
  `(f ∘ τ)^*𝒜 ≅ τ^*(f^*𝒜)` of the restriction datum of Stacks 084A
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.quadrupleRestriction`); this is computed on the
  quadruple `(1, f, ℒ, ψ)` the triple determines (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.
  quadrupleClass`, a bijection), where pullback and the restriction datum are defined.
* **The morphism.** A triple over `f` is classified by a morphism `T ⟶ Proj_T(f^*𝒜)` over `T`,
  the degree-one classifying morphism of Tag 01NZ
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.classifyingHom`), and by the second assertion of
  Stacks 084B (`Proj_T(f^*𝒜) = T ×_X P`) that is a `T`-point of `P` over `f`.
* **Naturality** is the third assertion of Stacks 084B: the comparison
  `Proj_{T'}((f ∘ τ)^*𝒜) ⟶ Proj_T(f^*𝒜)` is cartesian and is the identification of the
  restricted algebras followed by the base-change morphism of Tag 01O3, and the degree-one
  classifying morphisms are compatible with both, by the representation of Tag 01NZ
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.GradedAlgebraRestriction.classifyingHom_quadrupleClassRestrict`).

Neither the functor laws of `F₁` nor the naturality of the morphism need any hypothesis on `𝒜`:
both are read off in `P`, where the morphism is injective because the degree-one classifying
morphism is.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.relativeProjF1Functor`: the functor `F₁`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.f1ToRelativeProj`: the morphism `F₁ ⟶ P`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.yoneda_map_comp_f1ToPoint`: naturality.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.f1ToPoint_injective`: the morphism is injective,
  with no hypothesis on `𝒜`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.RelativeProjSituation.homEquivF1OfGenerated_symm_apply`: when every
  restriction is generated in degree one, the morphism is componentwise the inverse of the
  branch's bijection `RelativeProjPoints.homEquivF1OfGenerated` at `d := s.relativeProjPoints`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 085D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/085D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 084B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/084B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01O3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01O3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01O4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01O4)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

